// Refused: the only branch this lane can reach safely is "not cfn", which
// never calls ut_at (../../why/reason.id) at all -- two cases of it would both
// stay green with the `if(k_of(e) == "cfn")` check deleted outright, which
// is exactly the decorative case docs/TESTS.md warns against. The "cfn"
// branch itself calls ut_at unconditionally, which traps unless a case's
// `given` also ran ut_mark (../mark/); cfn_fixture (../../../fit/more/
// value/more/text/loc.id), the only "cfn" node this lane has, is built on
// fn_idx_fixture and never runs ut_mark. No fixture combines the two, and
// the lane's free function slots are already spent (see ut_note's note,
// ../why/note.id, for the same gap).
ut_case_val(int ci, int e) {
  if((import nkind)[e] == "cfn") {
    string s1_of_v = (import ns1)[e];
    if(find_str((import utname), s1_of_v) >= 0) {
      ut_named(ci, "this case passes '", s1_of_v);
    }
  }
} return void;
given ut_host_seeded given cfn_fixture given ut_add("fx_target", "asm 'in8'", "*") (0, (import cfn_e)):() then calls ut_named:(0, "this case passes '", "fx_target")
