// How the nodes of function `fnode` use the export `imp_nm`: 0 not at all, 1
// reading it only, 2 writing it too (node_import_use, ../../../given/then/more/
// calls/fit/use.id, says what a write is). A function's own node is created
// last of all its nodes, so they are the range from wherever the previous entry
// of `prog` ended through `fnode` (the same walk reach_funcs makes,
// mid/names/exports/reach/dead/sweep.id); a `then (import NAME)` check is
// refused under a function that only reads (then_imp_value, ./then.id). The
// range also holds the previous function's case nodes, none of which is an
// "import": a case's is a "cimport" (front/.../case/given/elem/cimport.id).
fn_import_use(int fnode, string imp_nm) {
  int f = 0;
  int lo = 0;
  while(f < len((import prog)) && (import prog)[f] < fnode) {
    lo = (import prog)[f] + 1;
    f = f + 1;
  }
} chain (int fnode, string imp_nm) {
  int hit = 0;
  while(lo <= fnode) {
    hit = node_import_use(lo, imp_nm, hit);
    lo = lo + 1;
  }
} return int hit;
given then_imp_fixture ("int", 1, 0) ((import then_imp_fn), "gx"):(1)
